1.	Introduction
Sound is compression wave that is perceived by brain via our ears which act like a drum.
a standing wave mode of a sound wave is known as a tone, different frequencies produce different tones. 
Music is the organisation of these tones in patterns known as rhythm and the combination of these sounds known as tone in rhythm sequencially and simultaneously.
harmony is when waves of compatible frequencies are played simultaneously. 

This project is to create a sound wave synthesiser that will be used in numerous sound and music applications.  ranging from complex music to general environmental sounds. 
with aims to ultimately descrbe quantum physics in terms of music. 

several paths will be considered that include generating static pieces just from code, to creating a console that can play sounds live. 
I intend to use this project as a learning piece to explore how the computer can generate these sounds from its hardware. 

